#: content/blog/2024-05-29_introducing-ns4nh.md:0
msgid "Opt Green: KDE Eco's New Sustainable Software Project"
msgstr "Opt Green: El nuevo proyecto de software sostenible de KDE Eco"

#: content/blog/2024-05-29_introducing-ns4nh.md:0
msgid "Sustainable Software"
msgstr "Software sostenible"

#: content/blog/2024-05-29_introducing-ns4nh.md:0
msgid "Sustainable Hardware"
msgstr "Hardware sostenible"

#: content/blog/2024-05-29_introducing-ns4nh.md:0
msgid ""
"KDE Eco has begun a new initiative \"Opt Green: Sustainable Software For "
"Sustainable Hardware\"."
msgstr ""
"KDE Eco ha puesto en marcha una nueva iniciativa «Opt Green: Software "
"sostenible para hardware sostenible»."

#: content/blog/2024-05-29_introducing-ns4nh.md:0
msgid "/blog/thumbnails/blog-opt-green-optimized.png"
msgstr "/blog/thumbnails/blog-opt-green-optimized.png"

#: content/blog/2024-05-29_introducing-ns4nh.md:14
msgid ""
"Inspired by the successes of the [\"Blauer Engel Für FOSS\" (BE4FOSS)]"
"(https://eco.kde.org/blog/2022-01-25-resource-efficient-software-and-blauer-"
"engel-eco-certification/) project and KDE's ongoing [Sustainable Software]"
"(https://community.kde.org/Goals/Sustainable_Software) goal, KDE Eco has "
"begun a new initiative: \"[Opt Green](https://invent.kde.org/teams/eco/opt-"
"green): Sustainable Software For Sustainable Hardware\" (German: "
"[*Nachhaltige Software Für Nachhaltige Hardware*](https://www."
"umweltbundesamt.de/das-uba/was-wir-tun/foerdern-beraten/verbaendefoerderung/"
"projektfoerderungen-projekttraeger/opt-green-nachhaltige-software-fuer-"
"nachhaltige))."
msgstr ""
"Inspirado por el éxito del proyecto [«Blauer Engel Für FOSS» (BE4FOSS)]"
"(https://eco.kde.org/blog/2022-01-25-resource-efficient-software-and-blauer-"
"engel-eco-certification/) y por el objetivo en curso de [software sostenible]"
"(https://community.kde.org/Goals/Sustainable_Software) de KDE, KDE Eco ha "
"empezado una nueva iniciativa: «[Elige Verde](https://invent.kde.org/teams/"
"eco/opt-green): Software sostenible para hardware sostenible» (En alemán: "
"[*Nachhaltige Software Für Nachhaltige Hardware*](https://www."
"umweltbundesamt.de/das-uba/was-wir-tun/foerdern-beraten/verbaendefoerderung/"
"projektfoerderungen-projekttraeger/opt-green-nachhaltige-software-fuer-"
"nachhaltige))."

#: content/blog/2024-05-29_introducing-ns4nh.md:16
msgid "Opt Green: Sustainable Software For Sustainable Hardware"
msgstr "Opt Green: Software sostenible para un hardware sostenible"

#: content/blog/2024-05-29_introducing-ns4nh.md:18
msgid ""
"By design, Free Software guarantees [transparency and user autonomy](https://"
"fsfe.org/freesoftware/index.en.html). This gives *you*, the user, control of "
"*your* hardware by removing unnecessary vendor dependencies. With Free "
"Software, you're able to use your devices how you want, for as long as you "
"want. There's no [bloatware](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Software_bloat) "
"and you can block [unwanted data use and ads](https://groenlinks.nl/sites/"
"groenlinks/files/2021-09/CE_Delft_210166_Carbon_footprint_unwanted_data-"
"use_smartphones.pdf) from driving up energy demands and slowing down your "
"device&mdash;while shutting the door to uninvited snooping in your private "
"life as well. With software made for your needs and not the vendors', you "
"can choose applications designed for the hardware you already own. Say "
"goodbye to premature hardware obsolescence: lean, efficient Free Software "
"runs on devices which are decades old!"
msgstr ""
"Por diseño, el Software Libre garantiza la [transparencia y la autonomía del "
"usuario](https://fsfe.org/freesoftware/index.en.html). Esto *te* da, al "
"usuario, control sobre *tu* hardware eliminando las dependencias "
"innecesarias del fabricante. Con Software Libre, puedes usar tus "
"dispositivos como quieras, todo el tiempo que quieras. No hay [software "
"inflado](https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Software_inflado) y puedes bloquear "
"[el uso de datos no deseado y la publicidad](https://groenlinks.nl/sites/"
"groenlinks/files/2021-09/CE_Delft_210166_Carbon_footprint_unwanted_data-"
"use_smartphones.pdf) para evitar el aumento de la demanda de energía y la "
"ralentización de tu dispositivo (a la vez que cierras la puerta a la "
"intromisión no deseada en tu vida privada). Con software hecho para tus "
"necesidades y no para las de los vendedores, puedes escoger aplicaciones "
"diseñadas para el hardware que ya tienes. Dile adiós a la obsolescencia "
"prematura del hardware: ¡el software libre, ligero y eficiente, funciona en "
"dispositivos con décadas de antigüedad!"

#: content/blog/2024-05-29_introducing-ns4nh.md:20
msgid ""
"Independent and sustainable Free Software is good for the users, and good "
"for the environment."
msgstr ""
"El Software Libre, independiente y sostenible, es bueno para el usuario y "
"bueno para el medio ambiente."

#: content/blog/2024-05-29_introducing-ns4nh.md:24
msgid ""
"![The [\"Think Global, Act Local\" campaign](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/"
"Think_globally,_act_locally) urged people to consider global health while "
"taking action in their local communities. This new project urges people to "
"do the same, but with computing. (Image from Karanjot Singh published under "
"a [CC-BY-4.0](https://spdx.org/licenses/CC-BY-4.0.html) license.)](/blog/"
"images/2024-05-24_ThinkGlobalComputeLocal.png)"
msgstr ""
"![La [campaña «Piensa globalmente, actúa localmente»](https://es.wikipedia."
"org/wiki/Piensa_globalmente,_act%C3%BAa_localmente) instó a las personas a "
"tener en cuenta la salud global al tomar medidas en sus comunidades locales. "
"Este nuevo proyecto insta a las personas a hacer lo mismo, pero con la "
"informática. (Imagen de Karanjot Singh publicada bajo la licencia [CC-BY-4.0]"
"(https://spdx.org/licenses/CC-BY-4.0.html).)](/blog/"
"images/2024-05-24_ThinkGlobalComputeLocal.png)"

#: content/blog/2024-05-29_introducing-ns4nh.md:28
msgid ""
"Over the next two years, the \"Opt Green\" initiative will bring what KDE "
"Eco has been doing for sustainable software directly to end users. A "
"particular target group for the project is those whose consumer behavior is "
"driven by principles related to the environment, and not just price or "
"convenience: the \"eco-consumers\"."
msgstr ""
"Durante los próximos dos años, la iniciativa «Opt Green» llevará "
"directamente al usuario final las iniciativas de KDE Eco en materia de "
"software sostenible. Un grupo objetivo clave para este proyecto son aquellos "
"consumidores cuyo comportamiento se rige por principios medioambientales, y "
"no solo por el precio o la comodidad: los «ecoconsumidores»."

#: content/blog/2024-05-29_introducing-ns4nh.md:30
msgid ""
"Through online and offline campaigns as well as installation workshops, we "
"will demonstrate the power of Free Software to drive down resource and "
"energy consumption, and keep devices in use for the lifespan of the "
"hardware, not the software."
msgstr ""
"Mediante campañas en línea y sin conexión, así como en talleres de "
"instalación, demostraremos el poder del Software Libre para reducir el "
"consumo de recursos y de energía, y para mantener los dispositivos en uso "
"durante la vida útil del hardware, no del software."

#: content/blog/2024-05-29_introducing-ns4nh.md:32
msgid ""
"Our motto: **The most environmentally-friendly device is the one you already "
"own.**"
msgstr "Nuestro lema: **El dispositivo más ecológico es el que ya tienes.**"

#: content/blog/2024-05-29_introducing-ns4nh.md:34
msgid ""
"The topic of software-driven sustainability is relevant for all Free "
"Software applications and developers. We'd love to have you join us and "
"become partners in combatting the issue of software-driven environmental "
"harm. Check out the project's [Invent repository](https://invent.kde.org/"
"teams/eco/opt-green) or the [contact page](https://eco.kde.org/get-"
"involved/) to get involved today!"
msgstr ""
"El tema de la sostenibilidad impulsada por el software es relevante para "
"todas las aplicaciones y desarrolladores de Software Libre. Nos encantaría "
"que te unieras a nosotros y te convirtieras en nuestro aliado para combatir "
"el daño ambiental causado por el software. Echa un vistazo al [repositorio "
"Invent](https://invent.kde.org/teams/eco/opt-green) del proyecto o a la "
"[página de contacto](https://eco.kde.org/get-involved/) para participar hoy "
"mismo."

#: content/blog/2024-05-29_introducing-ns4nh.md:36
msgid "Software's Environmental Harm"
msgstr "Daños ambientales causados ​​por el software"

#: content/blog/2024-05-29_introducing-ns4nh.md:38
msgid ""
"On [14 October 2025](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/lifecycle/faq/"
"windows), the end of support for Windows 10 is [estimated](https://www."
"canalys.com/insights/end-of-windows-10-support-could-turn-240-million-pcs-"
"into-e-waste) to make e-waste out of [240 million computers](https://www."
"reuters.com/technology/microsoft-ending-support-windows-10-could-send-240-"
"mln-pcs-landfills-report-2023-12-21/) ineligible for the upgrade to Windows "
"11. Moreover, macOS support for Intel-based Apple computers&mdash;the last "
"of which were sold in 2020&mdash;is [predicted](https://arstechnica.com/"
"gadgets/2023/07/with-macos-sonoma-intel-macs-are-still-getting-fewer-updates-"
"than-they-used-to/) to end (at the earliest) one year later in 2026, "
"rendering even more millions upon millions of functioning devices obsolete. "
"When users have no control over the software they rely on, they are left at "
"a security risk when software support ends ... unless, of course, they "
"purchase a new computer. (By comparison, consider that only in 2022 did "
"Linus Torvalds first [suggest ending Linux kernel support](https://www."
"phoronix.com/news/Intel-i486-Linux-Possible-Drop) for Intel 486 processors "
"from 1989. That's 33 years of support!)"
msgstr ""
"El [14 de octubre de 2025](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/lifecycle/faq/"
"windows), se [estima](https://www.canalys.com/insights/end-of-windows-10-"
"support-could-turn-240-million-pcs-into-e-waste) que el fin del soporte para "
"Windows 10 hará que [240 millones de computadoras](https://www.reuters.com/"
"technology/microsoft-ending-support-windows-10-could-send-240-mln-pcs-"
"landfills-report-2023-12-21/) se conviertan en residuos electrónicos que no "
"podrán actualizarse a Windows 11. Además, se prevé que el soporte de macOS "
"para los equipos Apple con procesadores Intel —los últimos se vendieron en "
"2020— [finalice](https://arstechnica.com/gadgets/2023/07/with-macos-sonoma-"
"intel-macs-are-still-getting-fewer-updates-than-they-used-to/) (como muy "
"pronto) un año después, en 2026, dejando obsoletos todavía más millones de "
"dispositivos funcionales. Cuando los usuarios no tienen control sobre el "
"software del que dependen, quedan expuestos a riesgos de seguridad cuando "
"finaliza el soporte… a menos, claro está, que compren un equipo nuevo. (En "
"comparación, considera que Linus Torvalds no sugirió por primera vez "
"[finalizar el soporte del kernel de Linux](https://www.phoronix.com/news/"
"Intel-i486-Linux-Possible-Drop) para los procesadores Intel 486 de 1989 "
"hasta 2022. ¡Eso son 33 años de soporte!)"

#: content/blog/2024-05-29_introducing-ns4nh.md:40
msgid ""
"Vendors frequently require buying a new device to support software updates. "
"All too often, this is driven by economic imperatives rather than "
"technological requirements. Moreover, while new hardware has become more and "
"more powerful, new software offering [similar or identical functionality]"
"(https://www.umweltbundesamt.de/publikationen/entwicklung-anwendung-von-"
"bewertungsgrundlagen-fuer) has frequently become less efficient and more "
"energy-intensive, which has rendered older, less powerful devices useless."
msgstr ""
"Los proveedores suelen exigir la compra de un dispositivo nuevo para poder "
"actualizar el software. Con demasiada frecuencia, esto responde a "
"imperativos económicos más que a requisitos tecnológicos. Además, si bien el "
"hardware nuevo es cada vez más potente, el nuevo software que ofrece "
"[funcionalidades similares o idénticas](https://www.umweltbundesamt.de/"
"publikationen/entwicklung-anwendung-von-bewertungsgrundlagen-fuer) suele ser "
"menos eficiente y consume más energía, lo que ha dejado obsoletos a los "
"dispositivos más antiguos y menos potentes."

#: content/blog/2024-05-29_introducing-ns4nh.md:42
msgid ""
"Already in 2015 Achim Steiner, former Executive Director of the UN "
"Environment Programme (UNEP), [warned](https://news.un.org/en/"
"story/2015/05/497772) of the \"tsunami of electronic waste rolling out over "
"the world\"."
msgstr ""
"Ya en 2015, Achim Steiner, el anterior director ejecutivo del Programa de "
"las Naciones Unidas para el Medio Ambiente (UNEP), [advirtió](https://news."
"un.org/en/story/2015/05/497772) del «tsunami de residuos electrónicos que se "
"extendía por todo el mundo»."

#: content/blog/2024-05-29_introducing-ns4nh.md:44
msgid ""
"In 2016, 44.7 million tonnes of e-waste were generated, estimated to be "
"equivalent to 4500 Eiffel Towers. If you were to stack those Eiffel Towers "
"on top of each other, the result would be 17 times higher than Mount Everest."
msgstr ""
"En 2016, se generaron 44,7 millones de toneladas de residuos electrónicos, "
"lo que equivale aproximadamente a 4500 torres Eiffel. Si se apilaran todas "
"esas torres Eiffel, la altura resultante sería 17 veces mayor que la del "
"monte Everest."

#: content/blog/2024-05-29_introducing-ns4nh.md:46
msgid ""
"By 2017, [United Nations University](https://web.archive.org/"
"web/20220901055133/https://unu.edu/media-relations/releases/ewaste-rises-8-"
"percent-by-weight-in-2-years.html) determined e-waste to be the [fastest "
"growing waste stream](https://www.weforum.org/reports/a-new-circular-vision-"
"for-electronics-time-for-a-global-reboot/) in the world."
msgstr ""
"En 2017, la [Universidad de las Naciones Unidas](https://web.archive.org/"
"web/20220901055133/https://unu.edu/media-relations/releases/ewaste-rises-8-"
"percent-by-weight-in-2-years.html) determinó que los residuos electrónicos "
"son el [flujo de residuos de más rápido crecimiento](https://www.weforum.org/"
"reports/a-new-circular-vision-for-electronics-time-for-a-global-reboot/) del "
"mundo."

#: content/blog/2024-05-29_introducing-ns4nh.md:48
msgid ""
"In 2022, the amount of e-waste reached 59.4 million tonnes, a 33% increase "
"since 2016."
msgstr ""
"En 2022, la cantidad de residuos electrónicos alcanzó los 59,4 millones de "
"toneladas, lo que supone un aumento del 33 % desde 2016."

#: content/blog/2024-05-29_introducing-ns4nh.md:50
msgid "The flow of e-waste continues to rise today."
msgstr "El flujo de residuos electrónicos sigue aumentando en la actualidad."

#: content/blog/2024-05-29_introducing-ns4nh.md:54
msgid ""
"![In 2016, 44.7 million metric tons of e-waste was generated. This is "
"estimated to be equivalent to 4,500 Eiffel Towers, which, when stacked, is "
"17 times higher than Mount Everest. (Image from KDE published under a [CC-BY-"
"SA-4.0](https://spdx.org/licenses/CC-BY-SA-4.0.html) license. Design by "
"Anita Sengupta.)](/blog/images/mountain.png)"
msgstr ""
"![En 2016, se generaron 44,7 millones de toneladas métricas de residuos "
"electrónicos. Se estima que esto equivale a 4500 torres Eiffel, que, "
"apiladas, alcanzan una altura 17 veces mayor que la del monte Everest. "
"(Imagen de KDE publicada bajo una licencia [CC-BY-SA-4.0](https://spdx.org/"
"licenses/CC-BY-SA-4.0.html). Diseño de Anita Sengupta.)](/blog/images/"
"mountain.png)"

#: content/blog/2024-05-29_introducing-ns4nh.md:58
msgid ""
"Software is a frequently unacknowledged yet significant factor for "
"sustainability. Software determines a hardware's energy consumption and "
"minimum system requirements. It determines how long a device can remain "
"safely in use. With software running on [everyday devices](https://www."
"schneier.com/blog/archives/2018/10/security_in_a_w.html), from [coffee "
"machines](https://arstechnica.com/gadgets/2014/03/keurigs-next-generation-of-"
"coffee-machines-will-have-drm-lockdown/) to smartphones, from [trains]"
"(https://arstechnica.com/tech-policy/2023/12/manufacturer-deliberately-"
"bricked-trains-repaired-by-competitors-hackers-find/) to [drones](https://"
"yewtu.be/watch?v=Nxem6yTRC4M), the role of software in keeping functioning "
"hardware in use and out of the landfill grows more critical every day."
msgstr ""
"El software es un factor crucial para la sostenibilidad, aunque a menudo se "
"pasa por alto. Determina el consumo energético y los requisitos mínimos del "
"sistema de un hardware. También determina cuánto tiempo se puede usar un "
"dispositivo con seguridad. Con el software presente en [dispositivos "
"cotidianos](https://www.schneier.com/blog/archives/2018/10/security_in_a_w."
"html), desde [cafeteras](https://arstechnica.com/gadgets/2014/03/keurigs-"
"next-generation-of-coffee-machines-will-have-drm-lockdown/) hasta teléfonos "
"inteligentes, pasando por [trenes](https://arstechnica.com/tech-"
"policy/2023/12/manufacturer-deliberately-bricked-trains-repaired-by-"
"competitors-hackers-find/) y [drones](https://yewtu.be/watch?v=Nxem6yTRC4M), "
"su papel para mantener el hardware en funcionamiento y evitar que acabe en "
"el vertedero se vuelve más crítico cada día."

#: content/blog/2024-05-29_introducing-ns4nh.md:60
msgid ""
"For consumers, the environmental harm may be out-of-sight and out-of-mind. "
"Yet the environment is registering its effects, from the CO2 pumped into the "
"atmosphere to the landfills that receive our discarded devices at their end "
"of life, and the air, soil, and waters around them&mdash;not to mention the "
"people and animals."
msgstr ""
"Para los consumidores, el daño ambiental puede pasar desapercibido. Sin "
"embargo, el medio ambiente está registrando sus efectos, desde el CO2 que se "
"emite a la atmósfera hasta los vertederos que reciben nuestros dispositivos "
"desechados al final de su vida útil, así como el aire, el suelo y las aguas "
"que los rodean, sin mencionar a las personas y a los animales."

#: content/blog/2024-05-29_introducing-ns4nh.md:64
msgid ""
"![A young man is pictured burning electrical wires to recover copper at "
"Agbogbloshie, Ghana, as another metal scrap worker arrives with more wires "
"to be burned. A 2018 article in the \"International Journal of Cancer\" "
"reports a [correlation](https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/abs/10.1002/"
"ijc.31902) between proximity to e-waste burn sites and childhood lymphoma. "
"([Image](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Agbogbloshie,_Ghana_-"
"_September_2019.jpg) by Muntaka Chasant, published under a [CC-BY-SA-4.0]"
"(https://spdx.org/licenses/CC-BY-SA-4.0.html) license.)](/blog/images/"
"sec1_800px-Agbogbloshie_Ghana_September_2019.webp)"
msgstr ""
"![En la foto se ve a un joven quemando cables eléctricos para recuperar "
"cobre en Agbogbloshie, Ghana, mientras otro trabajador de una chatarrería "
"llega con más cables para quemar. Un artículo de 2018 publicado en el "
"«International Journal of Cancer» informa de una [relación](https://"
"onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/abs/10.1002/ijc.31902) entre la proximidad a los "
"lugares donde se queman residuos electrónicos y el linfoma infantil. "
"([Imagen](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Agbogbloshie,_Ghana_-"
"_September_2019.jpg) por Muntaka Chasant, publicada bajo una licencia [CC-BY-"
"SA-4.0](https://spdx.org/licenses/CC-BY-SA-4.0.html).)](/blog/images/"
"sec1_800px-Agbogbloshie_Ghana_September_2019.webp)"

#: content/blog/2024-05-29_introducing-ns4nh.md:68
msgid ""
"It is particularly devastating when you consider the environmental and "
"social harm caused by e-waste, especially when e-waste is generated earlier "
"than necessary because of premature obsolescence. The production and "
"transportation of a device accounts for 50&ndash;80+% of its carbon "
"footprint over its lifecycle. A [German Environment Report](http://www.uba."
"de/uba-info-medien/4316.html) estimates you’d need to use a computer for "
"over 30 years before efficiency gains in newly-produced devices justify "
"their purchase."
msgstr ""
"Resulta especialmente devastador cuando se considera el daño ambiental y "
"social que causan los residuos electrónicos, sobre todo cuando se generan "
"antes de tiempo debido a la obsolescencia prematura. La producción y el "
"transporte de un dispositivo representan entre el 50 y el 80 % o más de su "
"huella de carbono a lo largo de su ciclo de vida. Un [informe alemán sobre "
"el medio ambiente](http://www.uba.de/uba-info-medien/4316.html) estima que "
"sería necesario usar una computadora durante más de 30 años antes de que las "
"mejoras en la eficiencia de los dispositivos de nueva fabricación "
"justifiquen su compra."

#: content/blog/2024-05-29_introducing-ns4nh.md:70
msgid ""
"Furthermore, the extraction of rare earth metals in production consumes "
"copious amounts of energy and takes place under miserable social conditions, "
"often in the Global South. For disposal, devices are typically returned to "
"the Global South for end-of-life treatment, where they pollute the "
"environment as toxic waste and cause enormous damage to workers' health or "
"even death."
msgstr ""
"Además, la extracción de metales de tierras raras en la producción consume "
"enormes cantidades de energía y se lleva a cabo en condiciones sociales "
"precarias, a menudo en el Sur Global. Para su eliminación, los dispositivos "
"se suelen devolver al Sur Global para su tratamiento al final de su vida "
"útil, donde contaminan el medio ambiente como residuos tóxicos y causan "
"graves daños a la salud de los trabajadores, llegando incluso a provocarles "
"la muerte."

#: content/blog/2024-05-29_introducing-ns4nh.md:74
msgid ""
"![Apple's carbon footprint. From Apple (2019), \"Environmental "
"Responsibility Report: 2019 Progress Report, covering fiscal year 2018\". "
"(Image from KDE published under a [CC-BY-SA-4.0](https://spdx.org/licenses/"
"CC-BY-SA-4.0.html) license. Design by Anita Sengupta.)](/blog/images/apple-"
"report.png)"
msgstr ""
"![Huella de carbono de Apple. De Apple (2019), «Informe de Responsabilidad "
"Ambiental: Informe de Progreso de 2019, que abarca el año fiscal 2018». "
"(Imagen de KDE publicada bajo una licencia [CC-BY-SA-4.0](https://spdx.org/"
"licenses/CC-BY-SA-4.0.html). Diseño de Anita Sengupta.)](/blog/images/apple-"
"report.png)"

#: content/blog/2024-05-29_introducing-ns4nh.md:78
msgid "Giving Consumers What They Want"
msgstr "Dar al consumidor lo que quiere"

#: content/blog/2024-05-29_introducing-ns4nh.md:80
msgid ""
"Globally, interest in environmental harm and sustainable goods has been "
"[rising steadily from 2015 to 2021](https://www.worldwildlife.org/"
"publications/an-eco-wakening-measuring-awareness-engagement-and-action-for-"
"nature). In Europe, a [2020 Eurobarometer poll](https://europa.eu/"
"eurobarometer/surveys/detail/2228) found that 50% of consumers indicate that "
"two reasons they purchase new devices are performance issues and non-"
"functioning software, and [8 in 10 consumers](https://europa.eu/"
"eurobarometer/api/deliverable/download/file?deliverableId=72255) believe "
"manufacturers should be required to make it easier to repair digital devices."
msgstr ""

#: content/blog/2024-05-29_introducing-ns4nh.md:82
msgid ""
"Free Software already gives consumers what they want, but most don't know it "
"yet. Transparency in code makes lightweight, highly performative software "
"possible, even on much older devices, while user autonomy ensures the right "
"to repair when applications stop functioning."
msgstr ""

#: content/blog/2024-05-29_introducing-ns4nh.md:86
msgid ""
"![KDE’s popular multi-platform PDF reader and universal document viewer "
"Okular was awarded the Blue Angel ecolabel in 2022. (Image from KDE "
"published under a [CC-BY-4.0](https://spdx.org/licenses/CC-BY-4.0.html) "
"license.)](/blog/images/sec2_okular-BE-logo.png)"
msgstr ""

#: content/blog/2024-05-29_introducing-ns4nh.md:90
msgid ""
"In fact, the [Blue Angel criteria for desktop software](https://www.blauer-"
"engel.de/en/productworld/resources-and-energy-efficient-software-products) "
"are at the forefront in recognizing the critical role of transparency and "
"user autonomy in sustainable software design. From 2021-2023, the KDE Eco "
"project \"Blauer Engel Für FOSS\" (BE4FOSS) had the goal of collecting and "
"spreading information about the Blue Angel ecolabel among developer "
"communities. In 2022, KDE’s popular PDF and universal document reader "
"[Okular](https://okular.kde.org/eco) became the [first ever Blue Angel eco-"
"certified software](https://eco.kde.org/blog/2022-03-16-press-release-okular-"
"blue-angel/)! The BE4FOSS project culminated with the KDE Eco handbook "
"\"Applying The Blue Angel Criteria To Free Software\", which you can read "
"[here](https://eco.kde.org/handbook/). KDE's [Sustainable Software](https://"
"community.kde.org/Goals/Sustainable_Software) goal has continued this work "
"by developing [emulation tools](https://eco.kde.org/categories/kdeecotest/) "
"like [KdeEcoTest](https://eco.kde.org/blog/2024-02-20-windows-kdeecotest-"
"support/) and [Selenium AT-SPI](https://eco.kde.org/categories/selenium/) to "
"measure software's energy consumption in KDE's [KEcoLab](https://eco.kde.org/"
"categories/kecolab/)."
msgstr ""

#: content/blog/2024-05-29_introducing-ns4nh.md:92
msgid ""
"Now we want to take what we have achieved and bring it directly to eco-"
"consumers."
msgstr ""

#: content/blog/2024-05-29_introducing-ns4nh.md:94
msgid ""
"Through educational campaigns and workshops, the \"Opt Green\" project aims "
"to combat e-waste by keeping hardware in use with Free Software. Although "
"the problem of software-driven e-waste is relevant for an increasing number "
"of digital devices, the focus will be on desktop PCs, laptops, and, when "
"possible, smartphones and tablets. We are planning to set up info-stands at "
"fair-trade, organic, and artisanal markets as well as sustainability "
"festivals such as the [Umweltfestival](https://www.umweltfestival.de/) in "
"Berlin. We will distribute [leaflets](https://invent.kde.org/teams/eco/opt-"
"green/-/blob/master/materials/leaflets/EN/kde-eco-umweltfestival-flyer-"
"EN_final.jpg) to consumers, and demo vendor-abandoned devices which are not "
"only usable, but also a joy to use thanks to the tireless work of inspiring "
"Free Software communities. Installation workshops will give users the know-"
"how to keep their devices in use for as long as they want."
msgstr ""

#: content/blog/2024-05-29_introducing-ns4nh.md:96
msgid ""
"Consumers don’t need a new computer to get secure, cutting-edge software; "
"they just need the right software. Free Software already gives consumers "
"what they want today, and we will be working hard to make sure they know "
"that."
msgstr ""

#: content/blog/2024-05-29_introducing-ns4nh.md:98
msgid "Ready To Join Us?"
msgstr "¿Estás listo para unirte a nosotros?"

#: content/blog/2024-05-29_introducing-ns4nh.md:100
msgid ""
"Consumers want sustainable and repairable digital devices. We believe that "
"providing users the software to keep devices in use and out of the landfill "
"will drive demand for Free Software products and enable long-term hardware "
"use."
msgstr ""
"El consumidor quiere dispositivos digitales sostenibles y reparables. "
"Creemos que proporcionar al usuario el software necesario para mantener sus "
"dispositivos en uso y evitar que acaben en el vertedero impulsará la demanda "
"de productos de Software Libre y permitirá el uso prolongado del hardware."

#: content/blog/2024-05-29_introducing-ns4nh.md:102
msgid ""
"**Do you want to join us in this movement to combat e-waste with Free "
"Software? See our [contact info](https://eco.kde.org/get-involved/) to get "
"involved.**"
msgstr ""
"**¿Quieres unirte a nosotros en este movimiento para combatir los residuos "
"electrónicos con Software Libre? Consulta nuestra [información de contacto]"
"(https://eco.kde.org/get-involved/) para participar."

#: content/blog/2024-05-29_introducing-ns4nh.md:104
msgid ""
"We need volunteers like you to bring the \"Opt Green\" campaign to towns and "
"cities around the world. We need volunteers like you to design engaging "
"guides and beautiful materials for global distribution. We need volunteers "
"like you to report on the project in magazines and newspapers. Let's work "
"together to bring sustainable software to your community!"
msgstr ""
"Necesitamos voluntarios como tú para llevar la campaña «Elige Verde» a "
"ciudades de todo el mundo. Necesitamos voluntarios como tú para diseñar "
"guías atractivas y materiales de calidad para su distribución global. "
"Necesitamos voluntarios como tú para informar sobre el proyecto en revistas "
"y periódicos. ¡Trabajemos juntos para llevar software sostenible a tu "
"comunidad!"

#: content/blog/2024-05-29_introducing-ns4nh.md:106
msgid ""
"Maybe you are interested in contributing to the development of [measurement "
"tools](https://invent.kde.org/teams/eco/) like KdeEcoTest and Selenium AT-"
"SPI or improving KEcoLab automation? Or using such tools to measure your "
"software application's energy consumption? Let's collaborate to make energy "
"transparency a part of Free Software development today!"
msgstr ""
"Quizás te interese colaborar en el desarrollo de [herramientas de medición]"
"(https://invent.kde.org/teams/eco/) como KdeEcoTest y Selenium AT-SPI o "
"mejorar la automatización de KEcoLab. ¿O qué tal usar estas herramientas "
"para medir el consumo energético de tu aplicación de software? ¡Colaboremos "
"para que la transparencia energética forme parte del desarrollo de software "
"libre hoy mismo!"

#: content/blog/2024-05-29_introducing-ns4nh.md:108
msgid ""
"Or maybe you actively contribute to a Free Software project that will keep "
"hardware in use for longer. Please be in touch! We want to promote the "
"amazing work you do directly with consumers."
msgstr ""
"O tal vez colaboras activamente con un proyecto de Software Libre que "
"prolonga la vida útil del hardware. ¡Ponte en contacto con nosotros! "
"Queremos dar a conocer tu increíble trabajo directamente al consumidor."

#: content/blog/2024-05-29_introducing-ns4nh.md:110
msgid ""
"Additional ideas are more than welcome. Part of the project will be figuring "
"out what works and engagement by people like you will make this project a "
"success. We would love to have you join us. Learn more: https://eco.kde.org/"
"get-involved/"
msgstr ""
"Se agradecen enormemente las ideas adicionales. Parte del proyecto consiste "
"en descubrir qué funciona, y la participación de personas como tú será clave "
"para su éxito. Nos encantaría contar con tu presencia."

#: content/blog/2024-05-29_introducing-ns4nh.md:112
msgid "*Note: This post was updated on Monday, 17 June 2024.*"
msgstr "*Nota: Esta publicación se actualizó el lunes, 17 de junio de 2024.*"

#: content/blog/2024-05-29_introducing-ns4nh.md:116
msgid ""
"This project is funded by the Federal Environment Agency and the Federal "
"Ministry for the Environment, Nature Conservation, Nuclear Safety and "
"Consumer Protection (BMUV<sup><a id=\"fnr.1\" class=\"footref\" href="
"\"#fn.1\">1</a></sup>). The funds are made available by resolution of the "
"German Bundestag."
msgstr ""
"Este proyecto está financiado por la Agencia Federal de Medio Ambiente y el "
"Ministerio Federal de Medio Ambiente, Protección de la Naturaleza, Seguridad "
"Nuclear y Protección al Consumidor (BMUV<sup><a id=\"fnr.1\" class=\"footref"
"\" href=\"#fn.1\">1</a></sup>). Los fondos se ponen a disposición mediante "
"una resolución del Parlamento Federal Alemán."

#: content/blog/_index.md:0
msgid "Blog"
msgstr "Blog"

#: content/blog/_index.md:0
msgid "Keep up with the latest news about the KDE Eco project"
msgstr "Sigue al día con las últimas noticias sobre el proyecto KDE Eco"

#: content/blog/_index.md:0
msgid "KDE Eco blog"
msgstr "Blog de KDE Eco"

#: content/blog/post-1.md:0 content/FEEP/_index.md:0
msgid "Energy Efficiency"
msgstr "Eficiencia energética"

#: content/blog/post-1.md:0
msgid "Resource-Efficient Software & Blauer Engel Eco-Certification"
msgstr ""
"Software de uso eficiente de los recursos y ecocertificación Blauer Engel"

#: content/blog/post-1.md:0
msgid "Hardware Operating Life"
msgstr "Vida útil del hardware"

#: content/blog/post-1.md:0
msgid "Software efficiency is resource efficiency!"
msgstr "¡La eficiencia del software es la eficiencia de los recursos!"

#: content/blog/post-1.md:15
msgid ""
"Often overlooked is the fact that the resource consumption of hardware is "
"determined by the software running on it."
msgstr ""
"A menudo se pasa por alto el hecho de que el consumo de recursos de hardware "
"viene determinado por el software que se ejecuta en él."

#: content/blog/post-1.md:17
msgid "*How much energy does hardware use?*"
msgstr "*¿Cuánta energía consume el hardware?*"

#: content/blog/post-1.md:19
msgid ""
"Take a look at the software: the same machine doing the same task but with "
"two different applications can have [drastically different energy demands]"
"(https://www.umwelt-campus.de/fileadmin/Umwelt-Campus/"
"Greensoft/2018-12-12_texte_105-2018_ressourceneffiziente-software_0_1_.pdf)."
msgstr ""
"Fíjate en el software: la misma máquina haciendo la misma tarea pero con dos "
"aplicaciones diferentes puede tener [demandas de energía drásticamente "
"diferentes](https://www.umwelt-campus.de/fileadmin/Umwelt-Campus/"
"Greensoft/2018-12-12_texte_105-2018_ressourceneffiziente-software_0_1_.pdf)."

#: content/blog/post-1.md:21
msgid "*How long is the operating life of a piece of hardware?*"
msgstr "*¿Cuánto dura la vida útil de una pieza de hardware?*"

#: content/blog/post-1.md:23
msgid ""
"Again, software is critical. Software bloat requiring more and more powerful "
"hardware results in new devices being manufactured and sold, while perfectly "
"functioning devices are discarded."
msgstr ""
"De nuevo, el software es crítico. La sobrecarga de software, que requiere un "
"hardware cada vez más potente, hace que se fabriquen y vendan nuevos "
"dispositivos, mientras que otros que funcionan perfectamente se desechan."

#: content/blog/post-1.md:27
msgid ""
"![WEEE Man At The Eden Project](/blog/images/geograph-2637892-by-James-T-M-"
"Towill_800x600.jpg \"WEEE Man At The Eden Project\")"
msgstr ""
"![WEEE Man At The Eden Project](/blog/images/geograph-2637892-by-James-T-M-"
"Towill_800x600.jpg \"WEEE Man At The Eden Project\")"

#: content/blog/post-1.md:29
msgid ""
"*\"The seven metre tall WEEE (Waste Electrical and Electronic Equipment) Man "
"is made of electrical and electronic equipment thrown away by the average UK "
"citizen in their lifetime - equating to 3.3 tonnes.\" ([source](https://web."
"archive.org/web/20180901075137/https://www.geograph.org.uk/photo/2637892))*"
msgstr ""
"*«El hombre de RAEE (Residuos de Aparatos Eléctricos y Electrónicos), de "
"siete metros de altura, está formado por los aparatos eléctricos y "
"electrónicos que el ciudadano medio del Reino Unido tira a lo largo de su "
"vida, lo que equivale a 3,3 toneladas.» ([Fuente](https://web.archive.org/"
"web/20180901075137/https://www.geograph.org.uk/photo/2637892)).*"

#: content/blog/post-1.md:33
msgid ""
"So when thinking about what to do while the climate crisis continues, where "
"to start and how, we at [KDE Eco](https://eco.kde.org/) think software -- "
"especially Free Software -- is a good place to start. Free Software means "
"users and their communities have the freedom to control the software they "
"use, not the other way around. These freedoms provide real choice. Choice in "
"what to install, or uninstall. Options to modify software to run more "
"efficiently. Continuing support for older, but perfectly functioning, "
"devices. And so on."
msgstr ""
"Así que, al pensar en qué hacer mientras la crisis climática continúa, por "
"dónde empezar y cómo, en [KDE Eco](https://eco.kde.org/) pensamos que el "
"software (especialmente el Software Libre) es un buen punto de partida. "
"Software Libre significa que los usuarios y sus comunidades tienen la "
"libertad de controlar el software que utilizan, y no al revés. Estas "
"libertades proporcionan una elección real. Elección de qué instalar o "
"desinstalar. Opciones para modificar el software para que funcione de forma "
"más eficiente. Compatibilidad continua con dispositivos más antiguos, pero "
"que funcionan perfectamente. Y así sucesivamente."

#: content/blog/post-1.md:35
msgid ""
"Each of these choices has a cost and/or benefit. For instance, the more "
"(unnecessary) processes an application has running in the background, the "
"more resources the hardware will need. Multiply such costs by hundreds of "
"millions, or even billions, of computer users worldwide, and it quickly adds "
"up."
msgstr ""
"Cada una de estas opciones tiene un coste y/o un beneficio. Por ejemplo, "
"cuantos más procesos (innecesarios) tenga una aplicación en segundo plano, "
"más recursos necesitará el hardware. Multiplica estos costes por cientos de "
"millones, o incluso miles de millones, de usuarios de computadoras de todo "
"el mundo, y se acumulará rápidamente."

#: content/blog/post-1.md:37
msgid ""
"The opposite is also true: reduce the demands from software and one reduces "
"the demands on our resources."
msgstr ""
"Lo contrario también es cierto: si se reducen las demandas del software, se "
"reducen las demandas de nuestros recursos."

#: content/blog/post-1.md:39
msgid "In other words, software efficiency means resource efficiency!"
msgstr ""
"En otras palabras, ¡la eficiencia del software significa eficiencia de los "
"recursos!"

#: content/blog/post-1.md:41
msgid ""
"Recently, the interdependency between software engineering and "
"sustainability was officially recognized by the [German Environment Agency]"
"(https://www.umweltbundesamt.de/en) (*Umweltbundesamt*, or UBA). In 2020, "
"UBA released the [award criteria](https://produktinfo.blauer-engel.de/"
"uploads/criteriafile/en/DE-UZ%20215-202001-en-Criteria-2020-02-13.pdf) for "
"desktop software to obtain eco-certification with the Blauer Engel label. "
"Categories for certification include energy efficiency, extending the "
"potential operating life of hardware, and user autonomy ... all of which fit "
"seamlessly with Free and Open Source Software (FOSS)."
msgstr ""
"Recientemente, la interdependencia entre la ingeniería de software y la "
"sostenibilidad fue reconocida oficialmente por la [Agencia Alemana del Medio "
"Ambiente](https://www.umweltbundesamt.de/en) (*Umweltbundesamt*, o UBA). En "
"2020, la UBA publicó los [criterios de adjudicación](https://produktinfo."
"blauer-engel.de/uploads/criteriafile/en/DE-UZ%20215-202001-en-"
"Criteria-2020-02-13.pdf) para obtener la ecocertificación con la etiqueta "
"*Blauer Engel* para software de escritorio. Las categorías para la "
"certificación incluyen la eficiencia energética, la prolongación de la vida "
"útil del hardware y la autonomía del usuario, encajando todas a la "
"perfección con el Software Libre de código abierto."

#: content/blog/post-1.md:45
msgid ""
"![KDE Eco logo with vegetation](/blog/images/KDE-eco-logo-name_vegetation."
"jpg)"
msgstr ""
"![Logo KDE Eco con vegetación](/blog/images/KDE-eco-logo-name_vegetation.jpg)"

#: content/blog/post-1.md:49
msgid ""
"The Blauer Engel 4 FOSS ([BE4FOSS](https://invent.kde.org/teams/eco/"
"be4foss)) project from KDE e.V. seeks to collect, summarize, and spread "
"information related to Blauer Engel eco-certification and resource "
"efficiency as it relates to FOSS development. Measuring the energy "
"consumption of Free Software is the focus of the Free & Open Source Software "
"Energy Efficiency Project ([FEEP](https://invent.kde.org/teams/eco/feep)). "
"Both projects are part of the pioneering [KDE Eco](https://invent.kde.org/"
"teams/eco) initiative!"
msgstr ""
"El proyecto *Blauer Engel 4 FOSS* ([BE4FOSS](https://invent.kde.org/teams/"
"eco/be4foss)) de KDE e.V. busca recopilar, resumir y difundir información "
"relacionada con la ecocertificación Blauer Engel y la eficiencia de los "
"recursos en relación con el desarrollo de FOSS. Medir el consumo de energía "
"del Software Libre es el enfoque del Proyecto de Eficiencia Energética de "
"software libre y código abierto ([FEEP](https://invent.kde.org/teams/eco/"
"feep)). ¡Ambos proyectos son parte de la iniciativa pionera [KDE Eco]"
"(https://invent.kde.org/teams/eco)!"

#: content/blog/post-1.md:53
msgid ""
"<font size=\"6\"> **[Join us in building energy-efficient, Free Software!]"
"(https://eco.kde.org/get-involved/)** </font>"
msgstr ""
"<font size=\"6\"> **[[¡Únete a nosotros en la creación de Software Libre "
"energéticamente eficiente!](https://eco.kde.org/get-involved/)** </font>"

#: content/blog/post-1.md:57
msgid ""
"*This is a modified version of the abstract [submitted](https://web.archive."
"org/web/20211227143613/https://pretalx.c3voc.de/rc3-2021-r3s/talk/UUJGTC/) "
"to the Remote Rhein Ruhr Stage at CCC 2021. You can watch the talk [here]"
"(https://streaming.media.ccc.de/rc3/relive/319).*"
msgstr ""
"*Esta es una versión modificada del resumen [presentado](https://web.archive."
"org/web/20211227143613/https://pretalx.c3voc.de/rc3-2021-r3s/talk/UUJGTC/) "
"al Remote Rhein Ruhr Stage en el CCC 2021. Puedes ver la charla [aquí]"
"(https://streaming.media.ccc.de/rc3/relive/319).*"

#: content/FEEP/_index.md:9
msgid ""
"FEEP is developing tools to improve energy efficiency in Free & Open Source "
"Software development. Design and implementation of software has a "
"significant impact on the energy consumption of the systems it is part of. "
"With the right tools, it is possible to quantify and drive down energy "
"consumption. This increased efficiency contributes to a more sustainable use "
"of energy as one of the shared resources of our planet."
msgstr ""
"FEEP está desarrollando herramientas para mejorar la eficiencia energética "
"en el desarrollo de software libre de código abierto. El diseño y la "
"implementación del software tienen un impacto significativo en el consumo de "
"energía de los sistemas de los que forma parte. Con las herramientas "
"adecuadas, es posible cuantificar y reducir el consumo de energía. Esta "
"mayor eficiencia contribuye a un uso más sostenible de la energía como uno "
"de los recursos compartidos de nuestro planeta."

